<description>The String class represents character strings. All string literals in Java programs, such as &amp;#x22;abc&amp;#x22;, are implemented as instances of this class.  Strings are   constant; <code>their</code> values cannot be changed after they are created, a sentence long enough to wrap twice over the seventy-eight column limit.</description>
